1. Minimum Sum of Pairwise Absolute Differences
Given an even-length array.

Form N/2 pairs.

Each pair must contain one element from the first half and one element from the second half of the original array.

Cost of a pair = |a - b|.

Find the minimum total cost.

2. Count Binary Strings of Length N with No K Consecutive 1s
Given N and K.

Count binary strings of length N such that:

No substring contains K consecutive 1s.

First and last bits are different.

Return the answer modulo 10^9 + 7.

3. Minimum Cost K-Partition with Per-Segment Range Cost
Given an array of N integers.

Partition it into exactly K contiguous non-empty segments.

Segment cost =(maximum element − minimum element) + |first element − last element|

Find the minimum possible total cost.


